@ref s 12(2)(c) (src:898-910)
GIVEN who IS A `Who makes the claim`
      against IS A `Whom the claim is made against`
      matter IS A `Matter of a dispute`
      `the employer is prescribed or belongs to a prescribed class of employers` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the matter is prescribed for the purposes of section 12(2)(c)(ii)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12(2)(c) the claim is made by an employer in a prescribed class against an employee about a matter the paragraph names` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The claim must be made —" by an employer (or the person entitled in the employer's place) against an employee of the employer; this claim is not made so
        IF NOT ((who EQUALS `The employer` OR who EQUALS `A person entitled under a written law to receive the amount claimed in place of the employer`) AND against EQUALS `An employee of the employer`) THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "concerning — (i) any matter specified in item 17 of the First Schedule or item 14 or 16 of the Second Schedule; or (ii) any other matter specified in the First or Second Schedule that is prescribed" (the matter is in the Third Schedule or in neither; limb (ii) is limited to a matter "specified in the First or Second Schedule")
        IF (NOT `s 12(2)(c) the matter is specified in the First or Second Schedule` matter) THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): who is "prescribed or belongs to a prescribed class of employers" is in regulations that are not among the sources
        IF `the employer is prescribed or belongs to a prescribed class of employers` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "by an employer who is prescribed or belongs to a prescribed class of employers"
        IF `the employer is prescribed or belongs to a prescribed class of employers` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
        IF `s 12(2)(c)(i) the matter is specified in item 17 of the First Schedule or item 14 or 16 of the Second Schedule` matter THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "any other matter specified in the First or Second Schedule that is prescribed for the purposes of this sub-paragraph" is in regulations that are not among the sources
        IF `the matter is prescribed for the purposes of section 12(2)(c)(ii)` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        IF `the matter is prescribed for the purposes of section 12(2)(c)(ii)` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "concerning — (i) any matter specified in item 17 of the First Schedule or item 14 or 16 of the Second Schedule; or (ii) any other matter ... that is prescribed" (the matter is neither)
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

