        -- limb (a) alone grants the permission ("or"), so it is tested first, and a limit that limb (b) needs does not matter to it
        IF (NOT (`the prescribed claim limit in section 12(7)(a) applicable to the claimant` EQUALS NOTHING)) AND `the total amount alleged to be payable under the claim for every specified contractual dispute and every specified statutory dispute` GREATER THAN fromMaybe 0 `the prescribed claim limit in section 12(7)(a) applicable to the claimant` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF (NOT (`the prescribed claim limit in section 12(7)(b) applicable to the claimant` EQUALS NOTHING)) AND `the total amount alleged to be payable under the claim for every wrongful dismissal dispute` GREATER THAN fromMaybe 0 `the prescribed claim limit in section 12(7)(b) applicable to the claimant` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the claim limits are prescribed under section 12(8)(e), and the Act states none; a total above nothing against a limit that is not known may or may not exceed it (a total of nothing cannot exceed any limit: "(if any)", fork F11)
        IF (`the total amount alleged to be payable under the claim for every specified contractual dispute and every specified statutory dispute` GREATER THAN 0 AND `the prescribed claim limit in section 12(7)(a) applicable to the claimant` EQUALS NOTHING) OR (`the total amount alleged to be payable under the claim for every wrongful dismissal dispute` GREATER THAN 0 AND `the prescribed claim limit in section 12(7)(b) applicable to the claimant` EQUALS NOTHING) THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where — (a) the total amount ... exceeds the prescribed claim limit in section 12(7)(a) ...; or (b) the total amount ... exceeds the prescribed claim limit in section 12(7)(b) ..., the claimant may abandon the excess amount" [ruled (b)] (neither total exceeds its limit)
