      `the Commissioner has inquired into and decided that dispute under section 115 of the Employment Act 1968` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 16(1) the claim cannot be lodged with a tribunal` MEANS
    IF `any proceedings relating to that claim are pending in, or have been heard and determined by, any other court or an Industrial Arbitration Court` OR `a claim lodged under section 119 of the Employment Act 1968 in respect of that dispute is pending` OR `the Commissioner has inquired into and decided that dispute under section 115 of the Employment Act 1968`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A claim relating to a specified employment dispute cannot be lodged with a tribunal if — (a) any proceedings relating to that claim are pending in, or have been heard and determined by, any other court or an Industrial Arbitration Court; or (b) a claim lodged under section 119 of the Employment Act 1968 ... is pending, or the Commissioner has inquired into and decided that dispute under section 115" (neither holds)
    ELSE JUST FALSE

