-- src:1087 | with a tribunal a claim for any amount relating to a specified
-- src:1088 | employment dispute concerning a matter specified in item 17 of the
-- src:1089 | First Schedule, or item 13 or 15 of the Second Schedule, that arises
-- src:1090 | from that dismissal, if —
@ref s 16(3) (src:1086-1090)
GIVEN matter IS A `Matter of a dispute`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 16(3) the matter is specified in item 17 of the First Schedule or item 13 or 15 of the Second Schedule` MEANS
    CONSIDER matter
    WHEN `A matter in the First Schedule` item THEN `sch 1 item number of` item EQUALS "17"
    WHEN `A matter in the Second Schedule` item THEN `sch 2 item number of` item EQUALS "13" OR `sch 2 item number of` item EQUALS "15"
    WHEN `A matter in the Third Schedule` item THEN FALSE
    WHEN `None of the matters in the Schedules` THEN FALSE

-- helper: the representations that bar or end a salary-type claim after a dismissal (s 16(3)(a), 16(4)(a)).
-- src:1092 | (a) the employee —
-- src:1094 | (i) has made representations in writing under
-- src:1095 | section 35(3) of the Industrial Relations Act 1960
-- src:1096 | to the Minister mentioned in that provision; or
-- src:1098 | (ii) has made representations in writing under
-- src:1099 | section 8(1) of the Retirement and Re‑employment
-- src:1100 | Act 1993 to the Minister mentioned in that provision;
-- src:1101 | and
@ref s 16(3)(a) (src:1092-1101)
GIVEN representations IS A `Representations to a Minister`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 16(3)(a) the representations are under section 35(3) of the Industrial Relations Act 1960 or section 8(1) of the Retirement and Re-employment Act 1993` MEANS
    CONSIDER representations
    WHEN `Representations in writing under section 35(3) of the Industrial Relations Act 1960` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Representations in writing under section 8(1) of the Retirement and Re-employment Act 1993` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Representations in writing under section 8B(1) of the Retirement and Re-employment Act 1993` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `No such representations` THEN FALSE

-- s 16(3): a dismissed employee cannot lodge a claim for an amount about item 17 First / 13 or 15 Second arising from the dismissal if they made written representations and have not withdrawn them or the Minister has decided.
-- src:1086 | (3) Where an employee is dismissed, the employee cannot lodge
-- src:1087 | with a tribunal a claim for any amount relating to a specified
-- src:1088 | employment dispute concerning a matter specified in item 17 of the
-- src:1089 | First Schedule, or item 13 or 15 of the Second Schedule, that arises
-- src:1090 | from that dismissal, if —
-- src:1092 | (a) the employee —
-- src:1094 | (i) has made representations in writing under
-- src:1095 | section 35(3) of the Industrial Relations Act 1960
-- src:1096 | to the Minister mentioned in that provision; or
-- src:1098 | (ii) has made representations in writing under
-- src:1099 | section 8(1) of the Retirement and Re‑employment
-- src:1100 | Act 1993 to the Minister mentioned in that provision;
-- src:1101 | and
-- src:1103 | (b) either of the following applies:
-- src:1105 | (i) the employee does not withdraw those
-- src:1106 | representations;
-- src:1108 | (ii) the Minister concerned makes a decision on those
-- src:1109 | representations.
@ref s 16(3) (src:1086-1109)
GIVEN `the employee is dismissed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claim is for an amount relating to a specified employment dispute that arises from that dismissal` IS A BOOLEAN
      matter IS A `Matter of a dispute`
      representations IS A `Representations to a Minister`
      `the employee withdraws those representations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister concerned makes a decision on those representations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 16(3) the employee cannot lodge the claim` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an employee is dismissed, the employee cannot lodge" [ruled (b)] (the employee is not dismissed)
        IF (NOT `the employee is dismissed`) THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording) [open question; reviewer expected JUST FALSE]: the bar is for "a claim for any amount relating to a specified employment dispute concerning a matter specified in item 17 of the First Schedule, or item 13 or 15 of the Second Schedule, that arises from that dismissal"; any other matter (First Schedule item 16, say) or claim is outside it, and the clause carries no "only"
        IF (NOT `the claim is for an amount relating to a specified employment dispute that arises from that dismissal`) OR (NOT `s 16(3) the matter is specified in item 17 of the First Schedule or item 13 or 15 of the Second Schedule` matter) THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "cannot lodge ..., if — (a) the employee — (i) has made representations in writing under section 35(3) of the Industrial Relations Act 1960 ...; or (ii) has made representations in writing under section 8(1) of the Retirement and Re-employment Act 1993" [ruled (b)] (the employee made neither)
        IF (NOT `s 16(3)(a) the representations are under section 35(3) of the Industrial Relations Act 1960 or section 8(1) of the Retirement and Re-employment Act 1993` representations) THEN JUST FALSE
        IF (NOT `the employee withdraws those representations`) OR `the Minister concerned makes a decision on those representations` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) either of the following applies: (i) the employee does not withdraw those representations; (ii) the Minister concerned makes a decision on those representations" [ruled (b)] (the employee withdrew them and the Minister has made no decision)
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- s 16(4)(a): a claim lodged by a dismissed employee about those matters is deemed discontinued if the employee makes representations under IRA s 35(3) or RRA s 8(1).
-- src:1113 | (4) Where an employee is dismissed, and the employee lodges with
-- src:1114 | a tribunal a claim for any amount relating to a specified employment
-- src:1115 | dispute concerning a matter specified in item 17 of the First Schedule,
-- src:1116 | or item 13 or 15 of the Second Schedule, that arises from that
-- src:1117 | dismissal —
-- src:1119 | (a) the claim is deemed to be discontinued, if the employee —
-- src:1121 | (i) makes representations in writing under section 35(3)
-- src:1122 | of the Industrial Relations Act 1960 to the Minister
-- src:1123 | mentioned in that provision; or
-- src:1125 | (ii) makes representations in writing under section 8(1)
-- src:1126 | of the Retirement and Re‑employment Act 1993 to
-- src:1127 | the Minister mentioned in that provision; and
@ref s 16(4)(a) (src:1113-1127)
GIVEN `the employee is dismissed and lodges a claim for an amount relating to a specified employment dispute that arises from that dismissal` IS A BOOLEAN
      matter IS A `Matter of a dispute`
      representations IS A `Representations to a Minister`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 16(4)(a) the claim is deemed to be discontinued` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an employee is dismissed, and the employee lodges with a tribunal a claim ... concerning a matter specified in item 17 of the First Schedule, or item 13 or 15 of the Second Schedule" [ruled (b)] (the matter is part of the "Where" clause here)
        IF NOT (`the employee is dismissed and lodges a claim for an amount relating to a specified employment dispute that arises from that dismissal` AND `s 16(3) the matter is specified in item 17 of the First Schedule or item 13 or 15 of the Second Schedule` matter) THEN JUST FALSE
        IF `s 16(3)(a) the representations are under section 35(3) of the Industrial Relations Act 1960 or section 8(1) of the Retirement and Re-employment Act 1993` representations THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the claim is deemed to be discontinued, if the employee makes representations in writing under section 35(3) ... or section 8(1)" (the employee makes none)
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- s 16(4)(b): ... with effect from the date on which the employee makes those representations.
-- src:1132 | (b) the claim is deemed to be discontinued with effect from the
-- src:1133 | date on which the employee makes those representations.
@ref s 16(4)(b) (src:1132-1133)
GIVEN `the claim is deemed to be discontinued under section 16(4)(a)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the employee makes those representations` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 16(4)(b) the date with effect from which the claim is deemed to be discontinued` MEANS
    IF `the claim is deemed to be discontinued under section 16(4)(a)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST `the date on which the employee makes those representations`
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording) [no yes-or-no]: the date is that of the representations that discontinue the claim under (a); the function returns a date, so there is no JUST FALSE to give
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 16(5): a dismissed employee cannot lodge a claim relating to a wrongful dismissal dispute if they made representations under IRA s 35(3) and have not withdrawn them or the Minister has decided.
