      `the claim relates to a wrongful dismissal dispute` IS A BOOLEAN
      representations IS A `Representations to a Minister`
      `the employee withdraws those representations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister concerned makes a decision on those representations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 16(5) the employee cannot lodge the claim relating to a wrongful dismissal dispute` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an employee is dismissed, the employee cannot lodge" [ruled (b)] (the employee is not dismissed)
        IF (NOT `the employee is dismissed`) THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording) [scope limit, ruled (c)]: the bar is for "a claim relating to a wrongful dismissal dispute"; any other claim is not spoken to
        IF (NOT `the claim relates to a wrongful dismissal dispute`) THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "cannot lodge with a tribunal a claim relating to a wrongful dismissal dispute, if — (a) the employee has made representations in writing under section 35(3) of the Industrial Relations Act 1960" [ruled (b)] (the representations were made under another provision, or none were made)
        IF (NOT (representations EQUALS `Representations in writing under section 35(3) of the Industrial Relations Act 1960`)) THEN JUST FALSE
        IF (NOT `the employee withdraws those representations`) OR `the Minister concerned makes a decision on those representations` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) either of the following applies: (i) the employee does not withdraw those representations; (ii) the Minister concerned makes a decision on those representations" [ruled (b)] (the employee withdrew them and the Minister has made no decision)
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

